Z||000001||WampusCat||12-15-2001||06:12 PM||||The previous owner put one on my Toyota PU.  I can tell a difference in how smooth the engine accelerates and it seems quicker with the Jacobs than the stock coil.  The stock coil was left in place so I just have to move the coil wire to switch between stock and Jacobs.  I've never done any tests with a stopwatch or anything.  There's sort of a mini-review here: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/mod.Jacobs-ignition.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/mod.Jacobs-ignition.html</A>  <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/Ray%20Paulk%20Article%20-%20Ignition%20Systems.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/Ray%20Paulk%20Article%20-%20Ignition%20Systems.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Earl||12-15-2001||09:16 PM||||anyone else?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||chester||12-16-2001||09:30 AM||||Sorry but my experience was not so good.  I bought a setup from them for my Chevy S-10 Blazer and it was a waste of money IMHO.  The computer fried on me within 8 months. Go out to start the truck and no joy. I paid a WAD of cash for it.  Won't go there again.<P>Rob D.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">       <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
